    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504-a3">

                <pb facs="0796" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg668"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 3,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">High Excellency</hi>: I am directed by the President
                    of the United States of America to express his heartfelt thanks, and those of
                    the people of the United States, for the honors shown by yourself and the
                    officers under your command to the remains of the late Lieutenant-Commander De
                    Long, of the United States Navy, and his companions of the Jeannette Arctic
                    exploring expedition on their passage through Siberia, which will ever be
                    remembered with appreciation and gratitude by this nation and serve to
                    strengthen the feelings of friendship and good will already existing between the
                    Empire of Russia and the United States of America.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, high excellency, the assurances of my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His high excellency Lieut. Gen. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dmitri
                            Gavrilovitch Anuchin</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Governor-General,
                            Irkutsk.</hi></p>
                    <p>The same letter sent to the following: <list>
                            <item>His high excellency Lieut. Gen. Guerassin Alexéievitch Kalpoffsky,
                                governor general, Omsk.</item>
                            <item>His excellency Maj. Gen. Serge Ivanovitch Nassovich, governor,
                                Irkutsk.</item>
                            <item>M. Demidoif, mayor of Irkutsk, Irkutsk.</item>
                            <item>His excellency the Counsellor of State, Vasili Ivanovitch
                                Mertsaloff, Tomsk.</item>
                        </list></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
